4. Add Automatic turn-around

Introduce a new human-player gameplay setting:

Automatic turn-around

This is an orientation feature, not a movement or attack-assistance feature.

Required functionality

When enabled, the player’s fighter automatically faces the closest valid enemy.

Examples:

Enemy on the right

The player’s fighter faces right.

Enemy on the left

The player’s fighter faces left.

Enemy moves behind the player

The fighter automatically turns to face the enemy, subject to the existing rules for direction-locked actions.

Player stands still

The fighter continues facing the enemy without requiring movement input.

Player moves away from the enemy

The player can still move away normally while the fighter visually faces the enemy when eligible.

Enemy crosses from one side to another

The fighter updates its facing without requiring the player to press the opposite direction.

Player jumps

Automatic facing continues to work in the air.

Enemy is removed or unavailable

The fighter retains its current facing rather than rapidly switching directions or producing errors.

Important restriction

Automatic turn-around must only change fighter orientation.

It must never:

* Move the fighter toward an enemy.
* Change horizontal or vertical velocity.
* Automatically Dash or jump.
* Automatically attack.
* Automatically start a combo.
* Alter Energy.
* Modify attack damage.
* Change movement speed.
* Teleport or reposition the fighter.
* Grant additional attack range.
* Override normal hitstun or recovery rules.

The player retains complete control over movement and attacks.

